    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-m/q4",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q4-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The table below shows the length of time, rounded to the nearest minute, spent by a group of patients for their dentist&#x27;s check up visit. One of the frequencies is given as a positive constant k . Time (nearest minute) 2 - 6 7 - 11 12 - 16 17 - 31 32 - 36 Number of Patients 6 15 k 24 12 Determine the standard deviation of these times, given that the mean of these times is 18.6 minutes. ( ) 8\" style=\"--madas-width:585.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q4-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:593.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q4-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"The midpoints are 4, 9, 14, 24, 34. [B1] [A1] The total frequency is 6 + 15 + k + 24 + 12 = 57 + k, and the weighted total is 6(4) + 15(9) + 14k + 24(24) + 12(34) = 1143 + 14k. From the given mean, 1143 + 14k = 18.6, 4.6k = 82.8, k = 18. [M1] [A1] 57 + k Cross-multiplication gives 1143 + 14k = 1060.2 + 18.6k, hence 82.8 = 4.6k. The second-moment total is 6(42) + 15(92) + 18(142) + 24(242) + 12(342). Thus P f = 75 [A1] and P fx2 = 32535. [A1] The grouped standard deviation is √ r32535 −18.62 = 87.84 ≈9.37 min . [M1] [A1] 75\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 4 is 8 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The table below shows the length of time, rounded to the nearest minute, spent by a group of patients for their dentist's check up visit. One of the frequencies is given as a positive constant k . Time (nearest minute) 2 - 6 7 - 11 12 - 16 17 - 31 32 - 36 Number of Patients 6 15 k 24 12 Determine the standard deviation of these times, given that the mean of these times is 18.6 minutes. ( ) 8 "
