    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-m/q5",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q5-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The volume of still water in Ebian bottles is Normally distributed with mean 502 ml and standard deviation 2.5 ml. A bottle of Ebian still water is selected at random. a) Determine the probability that the bottle will contain ... ( ) 2 i.    ... less than 506 ml. ( ) 2 ii.    ... less than 495 ml. ( ) 2 iii.    ... between 495 ml and  506 ml. ( ) 1 iv.    ... exactly 500 ml. ( ) 2 v.    ... 502 ml, correct to nearest ml.\" style=\"--madas-width:582.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q5-question-2.svg\" alt=\"The volume of sparkling water in Ebian bottles is Normally distributed with mean µ ml and standard deviation σ ml. It is known that 2.5% of these bottles contain more than 503.5 ml and 2.5% of these bottles contain less than 498.5 ml. ( ) 4 b) Determine the value of σ .\" style=\"--madas-width:600.1px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q5-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) For the still-water volume X, standardise with Z = (X −502)/2.5.\" style=\"--madas-width:517.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q5-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(i) P(X &lt; 506) = Φ(1.6) ≈0.9452 . [M1] [A1] (ii) P(X &lt; 495) = Φ(−2.8) ≈0.0026 . [M1] [A1] (iii) P(495 &lt; X &lt; 506) = Φ(1.6) −Φ(−2.8) ≈0.9426 . [M1] [A1] (iv) A continuous distribution assigns probability 0 to X = 500. [A1] (v) The two unrounded endpoints standardise to (501.5 −502)/2.5 = −0.2 and (502.5 −502)/2.5 = 0.2. The rounding interval is 501.5 ≤X &lt; 502.5, [A1] so the probability is Φ(0.2) −Φ(−0.2) ≈0.1585 . [A1] (b) The 2.5% and 97.5% quantiles are symmetric about\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q5-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"µ = (498.5 + 503.5)/2 . [B1] = 501 The source also gives the lower-bound equation 498.5 = µ −1.95996σ. Subtracting this from 503.5 = µ + 1.95996σ gives 5 = 3.91992σ. As (503.5 −501)/σ = Φ−1(0.975) ≈1.95996, [A1] σ ≈1.28 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 5 is 13 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The volume of still water in Ebian bottles is Normally distributed with mean 502 ml and standard deviation 2.5 ml. A bottle of Ebian still water is selected at random. a) Determine the probability that the bottle will contain ... ( ) 2 i.    ... less than 506 ml. ( ) 2 ii.    ... less than 495 ml. ( ) 2 iii.    ... between 495 ml and  506 ml. ( ) 1 iv.    ... exactly 500 ml. ( ) 2 v.    ... 502 ml, correct to nearest ml. The volume of sparkling water in Ebian bottles is Normally distributed with mean µ ml and standard deviation σ ml. It is known that 2.5% of these bottles contain more than 503.5 ml and 2.5% of these bottles contain less than 498.5 ml. ( ) 4 b) Determine the value of σ ."
  },
