    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-m/q8",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q8-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The heights of male students in a college are thought to be Normally distributed with mean 170 cm and standard deviation 6 . The heights of 4 male students from this college are measured and the sample mean was 180 cm . Determine, at the 5% level of significance, whether there is evidence that the mean height of the male students of this college is greater than 175 cm . ( ) 8\" style=\"--madas-width:592.1px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q8-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"For the claimed threshold test H0 : µ = 175 [B1] [A1] against H1 : µ &gt; 175. [A1] Assuming independent observations and the stated standard deviation, under H0 the sample mean has standard deviation √ 6/ 4 = 3 cm. [B1] Thus z = (180 −175)/3 [A1] = 1.6667\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q8-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"and p = 1 −Φ(1.6667) ≈0.0478 &lt; 0.05. [A1] The upper-tail critical value is 1.64485. The observed statistic exceeds it, equivalently the observed mean exceeds 175 + 1.64485(3). Reject H0. [A1] There is evidence at the 5% level that the population mean exceeds 175 cm . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 8 is 8 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The heights of male students in a college are thought to be Normally distributed with mean 170 cm and standard deviation 6 . The heights of 4 male students from this college are measured and the sample mean was 180 cm . Determine, at the 5% level of significance, whether there is evidence that the mean height of the male students of this college is greater than 175 cm . ( ) 8"
  },
  {
    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-m/q9",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q9-question-1.svg\" alt=\"100 N 50 N 40° 20° 25 kg The figure above shows a small box of mass 25 kg , pulled by two light inextensible strings along rough horizontal ground. The tension in the rope inclined at 20° to the horizontal is 50 N .\" style=\"--madas-width:560.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q9-question-2.svg\" alt=\"The tension in the rope inclined at 40° to the horizontal is 100 N . The box is modelled as a particle experiencing a constant frictional force, where the coefficient of fiction between the box and ground is 0.2 . ( ) 7 Determine, by detailed calculations, whether the box remains in equilibrium.\" style=\"--madas-width:590.8px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q9-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"The vertical components of the tensions both act upward: [B1] [A1] The normal reaction is R = 25g −100 sin 40◦−50 sin 20◦≈163.62 N, [M1] [A1] so limiting friction is 0.2R ≈32.72 N. [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q9-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The excess leftward pull is 100 cos 40◦−50 cos 20◦≈29.62 N. [A1] For equilibrium, the required horizontal friction is the difference of the two pulls: Compare 29.62 &lt; 32.72; the static friction can adjust to the smaller value. The ground can provide the required 29.62 N of rightward static friction, so the box remains in equilibrium . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 9 is 7 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "100 N 50 N 40° 20° 25 kg The figure above shows a small box of mass 25 kg , pulled by two light inextensible strings along rough horizontal ground. The tension in the rope inclined at 20° to the horizontal is 50 N . The tension in the rope inclined at 40° to the horizontal is 100 N . The box is modelled as a particle experiencing a constant frictional force, where the coefficient of fiction between the box and ground is 0.2 . ( ) 7 Determine, by detailed calculations, whether the box remains in equilibrium."
  },
  {
    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-m/q10",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q10-question-1.svg\" alt=\"C A 30° B 3m 10kg The figure above shows a uniform rod AB , of length 3 metres and of mass 20 kg , smoothly hinged at the point A , which lies on a vertical wall.\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q10-question-2.svg\" alt=\"A particle, of mass 10 kg , is suspended from the end B of the rod. The rod is kept in a horizontal position by a light inextensible string BC , where C lies on the same wall vertically above A . The plane ABC is perpendicular to the wall and the angle ABC is 30° . ( ) 4 a) Determine the tension in the string. ( ) 7 b) Show that the reaction at the hinge has magnitude 98 13 N .\" style=\"--madas-width:600.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q10-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Starting with a good diagram: (a) Taking moments about A gives 3T sin 30◦= (20g)(1.5) + (10g)(3), [M1] [A1] so T = 40g = 392 N . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q10-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(b) The hinge components to the right and upward are √ T cos 30◦= 20 3 g [B1] [A1] and 30g −T sin 30◦= 10g. [M1] [A1] √ Numerically the components are 392( 3/2) and 294 −392/2 = 98 newtons: Squaring and adding gives g2(1200 + 100) = 1300g2. The resultant magnitude is √ √ √ q 3 g)2 + (10g)2 = 10g (20 13 = 98 13 N . [M1] [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 10 is 11 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "C A 30° B 3m 10kg The figure above shows a uniform rod AB , of length 3 metres and of mass 20 kg , smoothly hinged at the point A , which lies on a vertical wall. A particle, of mass 10 kg , is suspended from the end B of the rod. The rod is kept in a horizontal position by a light inextensible string BC , where C lies on the same wall vertically above A . The plane ABC is perpendicular to the wall and the angle ABC is 30° . ( ) 4 a) Determine the tension in the string. ( ) 7 b) Show that the reaction at the hinge has magnitude 98 13 N ."
  },
  {
    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-m/q11",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q11-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The standard unit vectors i and j are oriented in the positive x direction and positive y direction, respectively. Three forces F = 4 i + b j, F = 3 a i + 2 b j and F = 10 b i + 3 j, where a and b are scalar 1 2 3 constants, are acting at the points ( A 1,2 ) , ( B 4, 2 − ) and C − ( 3, 5 − ) , respectively. a) Given that the resultant of the three forces is zero, determine the magnitude and direction of the total moment of these three forces about O . ( ) 7 b) Find, by direct calculation, the magnitude and direction of the total moment of these three forces about C . ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:598.8px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-m/q11-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Worked solution diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:506.7px\"></figure>",
